<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hethum I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1213–1270</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hethum I was king of the Armenian Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> from 1226 to 1270, founder of the Hethumid line of kings. He submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and travelled to their capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karakorum">Karakorum</a> in 1254 to secure an alliance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a>. The alliance brought gains in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, but the Mamluks devastated Cilicia in 1266, and Hethum abdicated in favour of his son Leo II in 1269.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hethum-i.jpg" alt="Hethum I" width="200" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Maximus Rex at English Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hetoum_and_Zabel.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
